+A key consideration for differential expression testing with single cell data is the unit of analysis. 
+Analyses which treat individual cells as independent replicates do not account for biological variability, e.g. between different cells from different individuals or lines. 
+Such pseudoreplicate-based analyses have been shown to find a large number of false positive associations [Squair et al., 2021](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-25960-2), [Zimmerman et al., 2021](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-21038-1), [Junttila et al., 2022](https://academic.oup.com/bib/article/23/5/bbac286/6649780). Below, we show how pseudobulking can be used to account for such within-sample correlation. 
